s://api.github.com/users/pal1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/x-compressed","state":"uploaded","size":158887634,"digest":"sha256:2c465c8c4bed50fde97336c991319176c00bf865475734427edab58c2f348516","download_count":144,"created_at":"2026-08-13T12:39:56Z","updated_at":"2026-08-13T12:40:22Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/pal1000/mesa-dist-win/releases/download/26.2.0/mesa3d-26.2.0-tests-msvc.7z"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pal1000/mesa-dist-win/tarball/26.2.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pal1000/mesa-dist-win/zipball/26.2.0","body":"- Updated Mesa3D to [26.2.0](https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/blob/26.2/docs/relnotes/26.2.0.rst?ref_type=heads&plain=0).\r\n- ARM64 binaries are provided by mmozeiko [here](https://github.com/mmozeiko/build-mesa/tags).\r\n- Support for x86 32-bit build in MinGW has been restored but without LLVM support to workaround [#156](https://github.com/pal1000/mesa-dist-win/issues/156) so no openclon12, llvmpipe or lavapipe and performance is much lower for software fallback emulated features aka. NIR lowering in zink and d3d12 (both OpenGL and VA-API).\r\n### Feedback info\r\n- Windows 7 / Server 2008 R2 support remained in place for the time being as [this poll results](https://github.com/pal1000/mesa-dist-win/discussions/112) were 70% in favor of keeping support at release time.\r\n### Build script\r\n- Handle gamma build requirements.\r\n### Build environment updates\r\n- [MSVC](https://github.com/pal1000/mesa-dist-win/compare/26.1.6..26.2.0#diff-b4e71060df4527250a4a5597da15a5a7cddc32d054cb84a34e5b617ab5855b56)\r\n- [MSYS2 MinGW-w64](https://github.com/pal1000/mesa-dist-win/compare/26.1.6..26.2.0#diff-b2f0f98cfb30e2c28e1ffa79af21ddc4844345657e8ad07028bfe562d7a2fda7)"}